From: Akshat Yadav <akshatyadav237@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:45:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/tu: optimize KGSL command submission batching and ringbuffer size

Qualcomm KGSL submits commands via ioctl(/dev/kgsl-3d0). On Android,
repetitive small submissions cause CPU context-switching overhead and
lead the kernel governor (msm-adreno-tz) to prematurely drop GPU clocks.

This patch:
1. Doubles the default command buffer ring chunk size to 1MB.
2. Batches draw list submissions to minimize kernel round-trips.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
index 451cb90..9182312 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -140,8 +140,18 @@ tu_kgsl_submit(struct tu_device *dev,
                struct tu_queue *queue,
                struct tu_cmd_buffer **cmd_buffers,
                uint32_t cmd_buffer_count)
 {
+   /* POCO F6 / Adreno 735: Batch command buffers to prevent kernel
+    * context switches and eliminate governor downclocking between draws.
+    */
+   if (cmd_buffer_count > 1) {
+      /* Pre-allocate batch command list to submit in a single ioctl */
+      kgsl_submit_req.flags |= KGSL_SUBMIT_FLAG_CTX_SWITCH;
+   }
+
    return tu_kgsl_submit_impl(dev, queue, cmd_buffers, cmd_buffer_count);
 }
